id: pm-todos-checklist-hierarchy
title: Preview marked checklist hierarchy repairs before applying relations
description: "Acceptance: reindenting a marked child produces one native relation change; title similarity never chooses a parent; cycles and deleted parents refuse before writes; compact previews include affected ancestors and children only. Overlap rechecked: Markdown parsing and text/source sessions do not assign reviewed native hierarchy meaning. Reuse SDK graph topology validators, certified reads, verified native history and mutateItem; one field producer drives preview and locked writes. Native staged-copy preview limitations are tracked in pm-todos-hierarchy-readonly-preview. Selected targets are revalidated inside the native item lock; sibling targets retain a documented last-read window. No package journal or frozen recovery plan."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: "gh:unbraind/pm-todos#168",hierarchy,markdown,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-29T00:32:09.934Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T09:24:42.649Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[37]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T00:32:34.510Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against current core public declarations and sibling graph, CSV and beads docs: no marked checklist repair contract exists. Reuse previewItemMutations for native validation and update for persistence, RelationshipGraph for affected topology, verified history for revision guards. Core transactions serialize transactions only (upstream #1620); re-read every guarded target immediately before writes and document the remaining ordinary-writer window. No SDK pin change, no git requirement."
  "2026-10-29T00:41:16.972Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the shared relation planner, strict revision sidecar schema, native staged validation/update path, bounded receipts and hierarchy CLI. Targeted non-git tests already verify single-child reparenting, exact-ID selection, orphan/jump refusals and ordinary-writer ABA boundaries. Apply is deliberately per-item with truthful partial-progress receipts; it has no frozen mutable journal or package-owned lease, and the final SDK read-to-update window remains documented."
  "2026-10-29T00:53:46.451Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable copy, reverting rows() to retain baseline targets made the one-child reindent regression fail (changed 0 instead of 1). Restoring the implementation passed the same regression; the package worktree was not mutated. Linked pm tests passed (typecheck and reindent regression). Real public-corpus reads exposed native previewItemMutations EACCES on immutable copied files; follow-up pm-todos-hierarchy-readonly-preview records the exact public signature and searches. No validator bypass or upstream write was made."
  "2026-10-29T00:55:39.035Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public validation measured 104 native items, 104 exported rows, zero skipped, 11189 Markdown bytes and 12293 sidecar bytes. Unchanged preview returned 104 unchanged. Two changed-preview attempts returned native EACCES, retained as a typed SDK limitation; every copied byte remained unchanged, with no git executable available. The corpus came from committed public main at d1202cf41d538ea11dc9a8967c6aabe64a9cf002. Source was only read through git archive."
  "2026-10-29T01:08:15.514Z",codex-agent,"Installed-path validation justified replacing unusable native staged-copy previews with shared core graph validation plus native mutateItem. Preview and the locked callback run one field producer. Every selected history revision is verified again inside the target item lock, and sibling-target races retain their documented last-read window. Host commands use the injected certified reader. The model now also covers moving an existing blocker between two parents, not only add/remove, so the old dependency is removed exactly once."
  "2026-10-29T01:08:54.442Z",codex-agent,"The final public read-only corpus validation now succeeds on both unchanged and changed previews: 104/104 rows exported, zero skipped, 104 unchanged; one relation proposal affects two rows in a 265-byte JSON receipt. No copied bytes changed and git was absent from PATH. Native staged-copy limitations remain a separate follow-up; the feature's shared native-field producer and SDK graph/mutation path avoid them."
  "2026-10-29T01:13:46.037Z",codex-agent,"The installed-artifact native-format state model passed all 500 seeded sequences: Markdown/tasklist projection, todo.txt, pi todo JSON, JSONL and checkbox; both importer names, sync, every exporter, producer validation, producer re-import, older input replay and CRLF variants. Full native documents were read back through the SDK and compared with an independent model, including preserved repaired parents, dependency annotations, body and every untouched native field. SDK date normalization supplies expected deadline values."
  "2026-10-29T01:23:11.579Z",codex-agent,"The final hierarchy model passed all 500 seeded sequences under random configured lifecycle registries and ambient focus. Targeted coverage measured hierarchy.ts at 99.70% lines / 90.98% branches / 100% functions and hierarchy-command.ts at 100% lines / 87.10% branches / 100% functions; full-package unchanged thresholds remain CI's gate. Packed npm-minimum acceptance passed on host 2026.10.23: two hierarchy rows, one applied relation, zero changes on replay; native source recovery and foreign copied-marker refusal also passed. A no-git CLI test fixture's missing declared peer link was corrected before final CI."
  "2026-10-29T01:26:58.528Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/pull/168. Final targeted no-git CLI, interrupted retry, multiple-blocker export and strict native ownership checks passed 4/4. The two 500-sequence models passed; npm-minimum packed acceptance passed. The released claim and append-only evidence are committed before the final CI push. Full npm and Bun release-gate receipts for the final head will be maintained in the PR; no merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-29T01:44:43.095Z",codex-agent,"The first exact-head CI run (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/actions/runs/40800575482, head 1c2903d) ran 447 tests: 446 passed and one new model assertion failed because the native writer added author_source, which the model's exact field set omitted. Coverage already met unchanged gates (99.25% lines, 93.58% branches, 99.71% functions on Node 26). The relation producer now explicitly declares author_source=asserted for its explicit author, and the model verifies it. The strengthened 500-format model with populated scope/source fields, sync-output replay and unchanged unselected parents passed locally. Final-head CI must rerun both npm and Bun gates after this correction."
  "2026-10-29T02:12:58.547Z",codex-agent,"CodeQL identified polynomial backtracking in the new rows() regex (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/runs/123214465842). Replaced it with disjoint linear prefix/marker scans. A million-space malformed row now returns orphan_row within the bounded child-process test on Node 24 and Node 26. In a disposable copy, reverting only rows() made that child time out after 15 seconds; restoring rows() passed. Fresh exact-head CI and CodeQL scans are required for this correction; earlier release-gate successes are preliminary only. Topology checks now run only for changed relations, retaining complete selected-revision checks and avoiding repeated whole-graph validation for no-ops."
  "2026-10-29T02:53:29.243Z",codex-agent,"Re-review: fixing the general rule that every durable prefix of a multi-item repair must satisfy native topology, even when a later mutation refuses ownership or is interrupted. The branch is clean and includes origin/main. Auditing all package mutation and transport paths; preview and apply will share a safe persisted-transition schedule and locked revalidation. GitHub currently lists only the already-fixed CodeQL regex finding; no additional non-blocking findings are supplied in the review payload."
  "2026-10-29T02:59:39.208Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: hierarchy.ts is the only package path that edits existing native parent/blocker/dependency topology. Its SDK export and CLI JSON/TOON commands share applyTodoHierarchy. sessions.ts and source-sessions.ts have explicit field allowlists excluding relationships (including compensation); import/upsert/sync preserve existing relationships; recurrence creates a new successor and edits schedule/provenance fields only. Replaced final-graph-only assumptions with a native-validated sequence of single-item graphs, plus validation of the exact live intermediate graph inside each item lock. No temporary edge mutations, blind rollback, workspace-isolation claim, or threshold changes. Regression covers inverse blocks edges, strict foreign ownership, both interruption points, current-state retry and every SDK boundary; the existing 500-sequence model now randomizes entire forests and checks every persisted prefix. Packed npm/bun local/global acceptance now checks JSON/TOON refusal, unchanged native histories, release/re-export and safe completion."
  "2026-10-29T03:18:37.757Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: copied the package and new regression into a disposable non-git scratch copy, reverted ONLY applyTodoHierarchy to the reviewed HEAD implementation, and ran node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=persisted test/hierarchy.test.ts. It failed in validTopology with ordering_cycle_created for the three persisted fixture rows (expected no cycles). A finally block restored the fixed function; rerunning passed 1 test, 0 failures. The working implementation was never reverted. The 500 native import/export/sync model sequences have also passed across all five formats; the expanded hierarchy model is still running."
  "2026-10-29T03:23:56.684Z",codex-agent,"Validation update: the focused two-file run passed 16 tests (including all 500 native-format sequences) and canceled the hierarchy model at its unchanged 1,200,000 ms limit after more than 450 sequences on the saturated host. Existing assertions, 500 sequences and timeout remain unchanged. New topology checks now run after every persisted write instead of redundantly rereading unchanged graphs at all four boundaries; the dedicated adversarial test still checks every boundary. Rerunning that model alone. All 3 linked pm tests passed through pm test --run --progress (tracking remains disabled by existing policy). Exact disposable revert argv used --test-name-pattern=\"every persisted hierarchy prefix\"; the linked command uses the equivalent unique pattern persisted. The packed checker passed refusal/progress checks but its initial projected PmClient.get read omitted blocked_by; the checker now uses readLocatedItem for the full native document, as the state models already do."
  "2026-10-29T03:27:11.173Z",codex-agent,"Packed npm-current acceptance passed on pm 2026.10.25 using the shipped artifact: hierarchy export/preview/apply/replay, strict foreign prerequisite ownership with applied=0 and unchanged full native histories, release/re-export and safe two-write completion. The receipt reports hierarchy_prefix_safe=true. Other existing source ownership, compensation recovery and foreign-marker checks passed in the same consumer. JSON/TOON and all six local/global npm/Bun scenarios will run in each CI release gate."
  "2026-10-29T03:28:45.363Z",codex-agent,"Fresh read-only public-data validation on committed pm-todos main input d1202cf41d538ea11dc9a8967c6aabe64a9cf002: 104 items, 104 exported, 0 skipped; Markdown 11189 bytes, sidecar 12293 bytes; unchanged preview 104 unchanged; changed preview 1 relation, 2 affected rows, 265 JSON bytes; no staged refusals. The scratch copy was non-git, read-only and had no git executable on PATH; all copied bytes and the source stayed unchanged. Final local typecheck, build:test, docstring gate (25 files, 152 declarations) and diff whitespace checks passed. Native state checks use readLocatedItem rather than lossy list/get projections."
  "2026-10-29T03:30:30.547Z",codex-agent,"Final local validation: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"500 seeded\" test/hierarchy.test.ts passed all 500 hierarchy sequences (1 test, 0 failures/cancellations, 387.7 seconds within the original timeout). Each actual persisted prefix is checked through native SDK reads; all original state/preservation assertions remain. Together with the earlier 16 passing focused tests, both 500-sequence models and all targeted scenarios are now complete. npm-current packed acceptance passed with hierarchy_prefix_safe=true; typecheck, build:test, docstring, changelog full/check, whitespace/privacy checks and all 3 linked pm tests passed. Re-review blocking class fixed across shared SDK/CLI/JSON/TOON paths; no other open non-blocking finding was supplied. Releasing only this agent claim. The final exact-head npm and Bun release gates (two workers, Node 22/26, six packed scenarios each) and run URLs/counts will be maintained on PR 168 after this final tracker commit; no merge or release."
  "2026-10-29T04:19:37.363Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 review: fixing two general rules: topology validation must use the complete registered workspace type universe, and native read/validation/history/write operations must retain the complete registered schema rather than a package-owned field allowlist. Branch is clean and includes origin/main. Auditing hierarchy, editing/source sessions, recurrence, imports/sync, CLI JSON/TOON and packed consumers for both classes. GitHub API review inspection is currently rate limited; the two supplied blockers are recorded here and any additional available findings will be checked after reset."
  "2026-10-29T04:48:41.240Z",codex-agent,"Class audit implemented: all direct native workflows now run under SDK runWithActiveExtensions for their explicit tracker; resolveItemTypeRegistry receives active registrations; default topology reads no longer disable extensions. Shared workspace.ts derives own field names from the same declarations index.ts registers, and unions every active registered field for native read/canonicalization/mutation. Hierarchy, editing sessions, source selection including compensation/recovery, and recurrence read/reschedule paths use this context. Removed extension suppression from the public validation readers and updated packed proof readers to use full native registered schemas. Foreign metadata remains outside each workflow write set. Real non-git regressions now cover a hidden registered-type bridge, strict unknown-field rejection with opaque foreign values, source compensation/retry, recurrence creation/rescheduling, and CLI JSON/TOON with no git executable. The existing 500-sequence all-format state model now seeds foreign registered fields under reject policy and checks full SDK native documents."
  "2026-10-29T05:01:17.783Z",codex-agent,"Both behavioral revert proofs completed in disposable copies, rebuilding dist after each mutation. Reverting only applyTodoHierarchy to the reviewed default-reader behavior makes the extension-defined bridge test fail because the cyclic proposal is accepted; restoring the function passes 1/1. Reverting only todoExtensionFieldNames to return package-owned names makes the registered-field regression fail with invalid_input after valid foreign-field rows are rejected; restoring the function passes 1/1. Commands: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=extension-defined test/extension-workspace.test.ts and the same command with --test-name-pattern=registered. The working implementation was never reverted. GitHub API access has recovered; inspection finds no additional non-blocking findings beyond the already-fixed regex thread."
  "2026-10-29T05:27:14.058Z",codex-agent,"Validation so far: all 500 strict native-format import/export/sync sequences passed with registered foreign fields, preserved relationships and full SDK read-back (818.9 seconds). npm-current packed acceptance passed extension_schema_safe=true and all retained prefix/ownership/recovery checks. Five retained hierarchy race/retry/ownership tests passed; retained source recovery tests and the existing source model are still running. The newly linked four-case extension workspace command hit its default aggregate 120-second runner budget after its first two cases passed, with no assertion failure. Its new link budget is now 360 seconds; source assertions, four cases and all existing 20-minute model timeouts are unchanged. The first three linked commands passed. The minimum published SDK 2026.10.23 declaration archive confirms runWithActiveExtensions and getActiveExtensionRegistrations, so the peer floor remains unchanged. Native close/terminal-update strict-field behavior on SDK 2026.10.25 is recorded on existing follow-up pm-todos-sdk-adoption-1025; no core changes were made."
  "2026-10-29T05:51:27.654Z",codex-agent,"Final local checks: the new four-case workspace suite passed via pm test --run --progress --only-last, including concurrent registry isolation, JSON/TOON no-git consumers, unselected registered descendants in affected scope, strict foreign-field preservation and recovery. The 500-sequence strict all-format model passed. Retained hierarchy tests passed 5/5; retained source files passed 60 assertions/tests with one existing 500-sequence model canceled by its unchanged 20-minute host timeout after 300 sequences; the targeted recurrence reschedule regression passed 1/1. No source assertion failed or existing timeout/assertion was weakened; full CI must finish the unchanged source model. npm-current and npm-minimum packed consumers passed both new extension_schema_safe=true and all earlier checks. Current import and recurrence create paths also explicitly unset parent/blocker/dependencies/sprint/release for independent births, and focused tests retain native independence under matching-author ambient focus. Fresh public immutable copy: 104/104 exported, 0 skipped, 11189 Markdown bytes, 12293 sidecar bytes, 1 change / 2 affected / 265 JSON bytes, all copied bytes and source unchanged; no git on PATH. Typecheck, build:test, docstrings and whitespace checks passed."
  "2026-10-29T06:25:53.928Z",codex-agent,"Final audit correction and results: after the earlier four-case run, adding ambient-focus creation assertions exposed SDK explicit_unset annotations in native birth history. The producer now explicitly unsets scope fields, and occurrence provenance verifies the SDK annotation against SDK-normalized birth state. A counterfeit annotation refuses without state changes. Final four-case suite passes 4/4 directly and through pm test --run --only-last --progress (58.6 seconds). Typecheck, build, build:test and docstring gate pass (28 files, 158 declarations). Separate disposable behavioral revert: replacing only creationMessage with exact message equality makes the strict foreign-field/focus regression fail; restoration passes the same test. The two blocking class regressions already each fail with only their responsible reader/field helper reverted and pass restored. No existing tests or thresholds were weakened."
  "2026-10-29T06:26:01.605Z",codex-agent,"Pre-push validation: strengthened seeded SDK-read-back model passes all 500 sequences with installed foreign types/fields, strict unknown-field rejection, old-input replays, all five formats, CRLF, custom statuses and ambient focus. Local npm-current and npm-minimum packed acceptance pass registered-schema and persisted-prefix receipts across supported SDK versions; final npm/Bun matrix will certify all six consumer scenarios. Retained hierarchy focused regressions pass 5/5. Retained source suite produced 60 passes and one cancellation when its original 500-sequence test reached the unchanged 20-minute saturated-host limit, with zero assertion failures; CI must supply full-gate evidence. Public immutable main tracker: 104 items, 104 exported, zero skipped; 11189 Markdown bytes, 12293 sidecar bytes, 104 unchanged, one proposed relation change affecting two rows, 265-byte receipt. Non-git read-only copy and source bytes unchanged. Strict tracker health: 10 checks pass, zero warnings; both touched histories preserve HEAD and main prefixes. No new non-blocking review finding was present in GitHub comments; prior CodeQL thread is resolved. Final exact-head gate URLs and counts will be maintained on PR 168 after this tracker snapshot, avoiding a metadata-only evidence loop."
  "2026-10-29T06:26:53.447Z",codex-agent,"Final recurrence compatibility checks pass 4/4: weekly completion/retry/chaining, foreign provenance/history refusals, replayed imports, and stored schedule/reschedule preservation. Command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"weekly completion|stored schedule receipts|bounded source metadata|replayed imports cannot\" test/recurrence.test.ts. Both review-blocking classes are fixed throughout the package. Remaining limitations are the documented cross-item last-read window and existing native SDK preview/lifecycle follow-ups. Releasing my claim with the feature in_progress for orchestrator verification; final-head CI results will be linked in PR 168."
  "2026-10-29T07:17:10.404Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 security boundary: untrusted committed tracker symlinks reach chmod during both read-only setup and cleanup in hierarchy, source-session and SDK differential validators. Rule violated: disposable-copy traversal must never follow foreign links for reads, permissions or cleanup. Audit also covers supplied-copy session/watcher validators, archive extraction, fingerprints, native SDK/CLI transports and packed npm/Bun consumers. The runtime hierarchy paths do not recursively change permissions. Plan: one shared validator-tree boundary rejects symlinks and special files before SDK processing, and permission cleanup handles only owned regular files/directories without dereferencing links; add safe outside-sentinel and disposable-runtime regressions for every caller plus behavioral revert proof. Main has not advanced (six commits ahead, zero behind); no merge required."
  "2026-10-29T07:34:16.097Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 class fix implemented in scripts/validation-tree.ts and all five public-corpus validators: complete no-follow preflight rejects symlinks, hard-linked files and special files before chmod or content reads; ordinary files are descriptor-bound and identity checked. Read-only guards retain their own descriptors and restore exact original modes without traversing current paths, including after root/file replacement. No runtime SDK/CLI command or packed consumer changes file permissions. Existing source-command and watcher transports already use no-follow, nonblocking descriptor reads; glob input selection is an explicitly requested read path, not a disposable-copy permission operation. The session copy retains exactly matching cache exclusions for fingerprint and producer. Independent candidate review checked setup refusal, failed setup, cleanup, replaced paths, dangling/cyclic/directory/proc links, hardlinks and FIFO input; no surviving static-link permission path found. No additional actionable non-blocking GitHub review comments are open."
  "2026-10-29T07:36:32.635Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 behavioral revert proofs completed in an isolated package copy with a disposable cloned Node runtime. (1) Revert only readonlyValidationTree to the previous recursive pathname chmod: replacement-root regression fails with changed outside sentinel modes; restore passes. (2) Revert only fingerprintValidationTree to file-only traversal: seeded link regression fails with Missing expected exception; restore passes. (3) Restore the original hierarchy validator functions from the reviewed head: the real CLI regression fails because the archived proc-self executable link changes the cloned runtime mode; restore passes across all five validators. The host executable is never a chmod target in these tests, and fixture finally blocks restore exact test-owned modes. Final direct suite: 5/5 pass, including 500 seeded variants, root/file replacement, FIFO refusal, matching cache exclusions, ten malicious validator runs and five legitimate native tracker controls. Existing untitled-row regression passes 1/1; real immutable public tracker remains 104/104 exported, zero skipped, one change/two affected/265 receipt bytes, no source or copy byte changes. No existing test or threshold was weakened."
  "2026-10-29T07:38:23.258Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 final local results: linked command node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/validation-tree.test.ts passes 5/5 through pm test --run --only-last --progress in 172 seconds, zero failures/cancellations/skips. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring (29 files, 154 declarations), whitespace/privacy checks and HEAD/main history-prefix checks pass. Strict health passes all ten checks with one existing stale-in-progress advisory, no integrity/history drift; unrelated tracker work was left intact. The reported archive-to-proc executable chmod is no longer reproducible in any of five validators; executable bytes/mode stay unchanged, and ordinary native corpus controls all pass. All three responsible-function revert proofs fail reverted and pass restored. Final-head full npm/Bun CI will run at unchanged thresholds and two workers; exact URLs/counts will be maintained on PR 168 after this tracker snapshot. Releasing my own claim, leaving status in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-29T08:31:20.317Z",codex-agent,"Round 4: the previous guard retained descriptors for chmod/read/restore but still resolved children through mutable ancestor pathnames. Before/after inode checks do not defeat an ABA directory-to-link-to-directory swap. Rule: every operation inside a confined tree must resolve each child relative to the verified open parent directory, with no pathname fallback. Audit will cover the shared collector, five validators, source-directory transport, SDK/CLI and packed paths. Plan: kernel descriptor-relative child lookups, explicit refusal on hosts lacking that capability, and adversarial tests at every traversal boundary including the exact ABA sequence, both read and chmod paths, nested ancestors, and a function-level revert proof. Main has not advanced: seven commits ahead, zero behind; no merge required."
  "2026-10-29T08:56:21.920Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 class closure now covers both validation-tree traversal and source-file transport. Added directory-scope.ts: each child and enumeration resolves through a retained parent kernel descriptor view; capability probes verify directory identity, and unsupported hosts refuse with remedies instead of pathname fallback. Source export prepares every parent before writes; nested preview/apply and the packed recovery driver use the same scoped opens. Logical names serve only display/collision/fingerprint labeling. Independent candidate review checked magic-link lifetime, no-follow intermediate opens, stale prepared handles, exclusive creates, hard links, parent aliasing, partial exports, closed-scope replay, host capability refusal and all five validator callers. Explicit operator-selected hierarchy/watcher paths do not assert this confined-child authority; their bounded final-file reads already use no-follow descriptors. Native SDK journals/leases, fields and scope semantics remain core-owned."
  "2026-10-29T09:04:26.238Z",codex-agent,"The class audit also found validate-sessions copying a verified source again through cpSync pathnames. Replaced that second traversal with copyValidationTree: reads use the same retained source descriptors, while fresh destination children resolve through retained destination parents. Copy and fingerprint share one exclusion list and collector. Added exhaustive copy-boundary ABA checks in addition to read/chmod checks. The direct scope tests pass 5/5 with 100% lines/functions for the new directory primitive; the seeded scope test covers 500 operations. The prior linked 11-test run passed, including all five validators and native source CLI controls; rerunning the final linked set now includes the new copy case. Packed npm-current passes directory_scope_safe, registered-schema and prefix-safety receipts, nested exports/previews, JSON scope refusals before outputs, replay and native recovery."
  "2026-10-29T09:11:12.932Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 behavioral evidence: in a disposable package copy, reverting only openTree makes the chmod ABA test fail on an outside-inode chmod and the read ABA test fail on foreign bytes; restoring passes both. Restoring the old source-command path resolver makes the real nested CLI test read foreign source text; restored descriptor transport passes preview/apply/replay with native fields read back through the SDK. A separate copy-reader counterfactual changing only its read from retained fd to the old source pathname fails the exhaustive copy ABA test; restoring the fd read passes. The old five-validator link/proc-executable regressions remain intact. No host executable or real tracker is mutated; all swap targets/sentinels are disposable and modes are restored in finally. Public immutable validation still reports 104/104 rows, zero skipped, one proposed change/two affected/265 receipt bytes, 11189 Markdown and 12293 sidecar bytes, and no source/copy byte changes."
  "2026-10-29T09:14:01.446Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 final focused run passes 12/12 through pm test --run --only-last --progress in 303 seconds: 96 read + 120 chmod + 236 copy before/after syscall boundaries (452 total), 500 scoped read/create/replay cases, capability/unsafe-path refusals, existing and nested native source CLI tests, 500 retained static-link cases, all five validator attack/control runs, and original proc-executable regression. Final private-copy owner-execution control passes separately after its creation-mode adjustment. New directory primitive targeted coverage is 100% lines/functions, 90.91% branches; full unchanged aggregate thresholds remain for CI. npm-current packed acceptance passes directory_scope_safe plus schema/prefix/recovery receipts; CI will certify npm/Bun local/global and npx/bunx across floor/pin/current hosts. Typecheck, test compilation, docstrings (30 files, 157 declarations), whitespace checks and strict health pass; health retains one unrelated stale-work advisory. All four current behavioral proof paths fail under function-level unsafe reintroduction and pass restored. Releasing my own claim, leaving in_progress for orchestrator verification. Final exact-head CI URLs/counts will be maintained on PR 168 after this committed tracker snapshot."
  "2026-10-29T09:17:31.446Z",codex-agent,"Before the final push, strengthened the adversarial matrix further: swap each nested ancestor too, rather than only the copy root. This catches a partial fix that anchors just the root while leaving deeper components pathname-based. Every nested preflight boundary is covered; root replacement also covers post-preflight reads/writes/restoration. Reclaimed my released item only to record and verify this additional test evidence; source implementation is unchanged."
  "2026-10-29T09:24:36.484Z",codex-agent,"Final nested-ancestor matrix passes 5/5 directly: 312 read + 330 chmod + 770 copy before/after boundaries (1412 total), plus 500 scoped operations and capability refusals. A further disposable-copy counterfactual anchors only the root while resolving deeper components by pathname: the nested chmod regression fails; full every-parent anchoring restored passes. This explicitly catches an incomplete root-only fix. The implementation is unchanged from the prior native/packed pass, apart from preserving the owner execute bit when creating a private validation copy, whose separate control also passes. Typecheck, build:test, docstrings and whitespace checks pass. Releasing my own claim again after this strengthened evidence; final CI will run all unchanged full-gate thresholds."
